==English==
{{was wotd|2025|February|27}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{compound|en|1|0|1}}, from the method of numbering courses in United States colleges, the initial or introductory course commonly being numbered “101”; for example, “Biology 101”.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adj|id=1006094113|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj|us=1}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˌwʌnəʊˈwʌn/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌwʌnˌoʊˈwʌn/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-101.ogg|a=GA}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|Canada|US|alone|or|postpositive|chiefly|humorous}} Of a [[fact#Noun|fact]], [[subject#Noun|subject]], etc.: [[basic#Adjective|basic]], [[beginner]]-[[level#Noun|level]], [[elementary#Adjective|elementary]].
#: {{ux|en|Geology '''101''' tells us that you can’t build a reservoir on sandstone.}}
#: {{ux|en|My dog flunked out of Crate Training '''101'''.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|actor=w:Jennifer Hale|role=Samantha “Sam”|title=w:Totally Spies!|season=2|number=21|episode=Ski Trip|writers=Holly Henderson; Liz Tigelaar|network=w:Teletoon|publisher=w:Marathon Media|date=Jun 22 2003|passage=Ugh! Crash and burn! Next year, I’m taking flirting '''101'''! I am so not good at this!}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2004|author=Daniel Dor|title=From Englishization to Imposed Multilingualism: Globalization, the Internet, and the Political Economy of the Linguistic Code|journal=w:Public Culture|volume=16|issue=1|passage=Companies sell directories, databases, reports, translation services, automatic translation software, and guidebooks for doing business away from home, which, in some cases, look much like simplified textbooks for Anthropology '''101'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|titleurl=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/a-class-in-nation-building-101/|title=Face the Nation|text="A Class in Nation-Building '''101'''": As the President tries to develop a new strategy in Afghanistan, I wonder if this is the real lesson that we've learned in Afghanistan so far: that nation-building, like charity, probably begins at home.|date=2009-11-01|work=CBS News|author=Bob Schieffer}}
#* {{quote-av|en|speaker=Norm Macdonald|title=w:Norm Macdonald Live|year=2017|season=3|number=11
|passage=I'm taking a fascinating class all about the Hollywood Freeway. It's called 101: '''101'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023-03-20|author=Rebecca Gillam; Bridie Wilkins|title=Alexandra Daddario and her PT on how she built her Baywatch bod + her 10 regular workout rules|journal={{w|Women's Health (magazine)|Women's Health}}|titleurl=https://www.womenshealthmag.com/uk/fitness/a39462034/alexandra-daddario-workout/|passage=However much you work out, but especially if it’s a lot, learning correct form and focusing on keeping your body safe is '''101''' — not just while exercising, but also how you move around day to day.}}

=====Usage notes=====
The word is used humorously or sarcastically with subjects, etc., that would never form the title of actual college courses.

